I am standing outside an old café in Mumbai.
This is a famous Irani café.
I open the door.
I go inside.
The café is very crowded.
I catch a nice smell of tea.
I look around.
The atmosphere of the café is very old and beautiful.
There are wooden chairs everywhere here.
Their color is dark.
There is a checkered cloth on the tables.
I look up at the ceiling.
There are very large fans there.
Those fans are turning very slowly.
I really like this place.
Now I want a place to sit.
I want tea.
I walk forward.
